    "title": "Atletico Madrid vs Barcelona LIVE: Champions League result, latest updates and fan reaction",
    "text": "Atletico ​Madrid reached the Champions League semi-finals for the first time in nine years despite a 2-1 home ⁠defeat by Barcelona in a thrilling encounter on Tuesday, advancing 3-2 on aggregate after their 2-0 first-leg win at the ⁠Camp Nou. Barca struck ​twice ⁠in the first half to level the tie. Lamine Yamal capitalised ⁠on a Clement Lenglet error to ​open ⁠the scoring in ‌the fourth minute, finishing neatly past goalkeeper Juan Musso after Ferran Torres set ‌him up.Torres then made ‌it 2-0 in the 24th minute, racing clear onto Dani Olmo's pass and driving ⁠the ball into the top corner. Barcelona dominated possession after the break and had a third effort ruled out for offside against Torres, while Pedri and Gavi controlled midfield.Barca finished with 10 men ‌after a last-man challenge brought ​a red card for defender ‌Eric Garcia and ⁠Atletico held on to secure a ⁠place in the last four against Arsenal or ‌Sporting who ​play on Wednesday ‌with the London side ​leading 1-0. Get involvedLeave a comment and the best will feature in our live blog. Be the First to Comment Atletico Madrid vs Barcelona latest updatesFT: Atletico 1-2 Barcelona (3-2 on agg)There we have it. Atleti are through. Just. They will face either Arsenal or Sporting Lisbon in the semi-finals. Atletico 1-2 Barcelona90+7 mins: Close! What a chance for Araujo, who has a free header as the cross comes in, but he nods over! Atletico 1-2 Barcelona90+5 mins: It’s all Barca now as Atleti shrink into their defensive shape. What is that, 8-2-0? Atletico 1-2 Barcelona90+1 min: Eight added minutes.Atletico 1-2 Barcelona90 mins: Araujo and Bardghji are on for the visitors, while Cardoso comes on for Koke. Atletico 1-2 Barcelona88 mins: Barca are short-staffed at the back as Sorloth gathers, and Molina is ahead of him if he can pick him out. He receives the ball having been in his own half when the pass was played, bearing down on goal, but his finish is rushed and straight at Garcia.Atletico 1-2 Barcelona86 mins: Barca are banging on the door now. Can Atleti hold out? Atletico 1-2 Barcelona82 mins: De Jong is on for Gavi.Atletico 1-2 Barcelona81 mins: Alvarez lines up the resulting free kick, but Garcia holds. Atletico 1-2 Barcelona80 mims: VAR is checking... and Garcia is sent off!",
